# Line endings are decided here, not by each machine's core.autocrlf.
#
# Several tests compare a file on disk byte for byte against bytes this code just produced: the
# frozen plugin API surface and the plugin.json schema golden (ADR-012, ADR-017), and the packaging
# scripts that must stay POSIX shell. A checkout that rewrote their newlines as CRLF failed every
# one of them.
#
# That is exactly what a Windows CI runner does - it sets core.autocrlf=true - and exactly what a
# developer with core.autocrlf=false never sees. The two disagreed silently until the test suite
# started running on Windows in CI, so the answer belongs in the repository rather than in each
# clone's configuration.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The two interpreters that genuinely need CRLF: cmd.exe misparses a batch file without it.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
